    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing on June 23, headlined by the explosive matchup between **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and Ryan Johnson. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a soft SP_xERA of 5.15 and a dynamic platoon advantage, making him our cornerstone play. He is flanked by **Kyle Tucker** (76.70) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), both of whom are set to capitalize on favorable park factors and the exploitable pitching profiles of Kendry Rojas and JR Ritchie, respectively. **Andy Pages** (74.01) also registers as a strong start, with his efficiency bolstered significantly by the 19% SP skill lift provided by the opposing rotation\u2019s vulnerabilities.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal start of **Drake Baldwin** (56.97) and the exclusion of **Josh Jung** (55.97) from the active lineup. While **Josh Jung** remains a high-floor asset, he was squeezed out by the optimizer due to a neutral platoon matchup against Sandy Alcantara and a sub-optimal park factor. Conversely, **Drake Baldwin** earns the start at catcher due to his projectable xwOBA and a favorable batting order position, though his status remains contingent on final lineup confirmation. We are also keeping a close eye on **Wade Meckler** (52.44), whose platoon advantage is helping him narrowly edge out bench depth like **Nasim Nunez**, even as **Nasim Nunez** possesses high-end speed that we weigh heavily in our scarcity-driven strategy.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the \"Lineup Pending\" status for nearly every position player, including **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.78), who carries a high weight today despite facing a middling Peter Lambert. While we are aggressively targeting the weak SP_xERA marks across the board, the weather and potential late-scratches\u2014particularly for **Coby Mayo** (56.48) and **Brayan Rocchio** (51.23)\u2014could force adjustments. We are essentially betting on our core of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill** to carry the load, banking on their platoon and SP efficiency edges to offset the risks inherent in today's pending lineups.",
